topic: "PF0 shared PR client repository-directory Path type boundary"
error_signature: "normal create-pr PF0 fails before any PR write with 'unsupported operand type(s) for /: str and str' when repo_dir / d receives the str returned by _git_toplevel()"
root_cause: "a boundary between Git helper output (str) and pathlib path arithmetic (repo_dir / d) lacked an explicit pathlib.Path conversion at the actual cmd_create_pr -> run_preflight callsite; shared controlled PR client defect, not any single library source issue"
durable_solution:
  - "at that callsite use the minimal explicit Path conversion: run_preflight(Path(_git_toplevel() or '.'), args.target, args.source) with the required import (from pathlib import Path)"
  - "prove the exact approved whole-file value (baseline e7d899d8… to fixed e9602421…, actually regression-verified)"
  - "run a local regression through the actual call path (real cmd_create_pr -> run_preflight receives pathlib.Path; original str contrast reproduces TypeError; fixed callsite eliminates it)"
  - "run normal non-bypassed PF0-PF4 (zero findings, zero network/API/credential access during validation)"
  - "restore temporary validation bytes byte-for-byte to baseline e7d899d8… before any later delivery; never leave the temporary patch in a release artifact"
impact: "this blocks every repository using this controlled client from creating a PR through normal preflight, so the remedy is reusable shared-client knowledge rather than a cute_tiled source change"
evidence_references:
  - "R21 PR-delivery first-error log SHA fb25420be4f080007a686d05dfc237a9599e38989f1551e1bdd22f9d99354251"
  - "R22 exact-patch log SHA 28b19031c8314719d06d5100a88174766fa4872421f466762552be21484742cf"
  - "actual-callpath regression SHA d069fd93be7949f91512da353e248fdb96941abf757125ba413f86e61dc02576"
  - "PF0-PF4 nonwrite validation SHA 1e24eff485ddbed0a16a4fae239e320b6d90e1d0ee09f5c98f565f4c00cc40e3"
  - "restore/atomicity SHA 2913a752f03f3aa5f6498a42dc8f2bb4e5474a4c50b27e365ae75333823168cc"
recovery_condition: "a subsequent, separately authorized delivery may use only the known exact fix with normal preflight, then must restore baseline bytes; a mismatch, PF0 recurrence, or any request for --no-preflight freezes delivery; never degrade to curl/raw HTTP/browser automation and never leave a client byte patch behind"
status: draft_pending_review